    <statement><p>Find the eigenvalues of <m>A</m>, given that <m>A = \left[\begin{array}{ccc}
9 \amp 4 \amp -18\cr
10 \amp 3 \amp -18\cr
5 \amp 4 \amp -14
\end{array}\right]</m></p>
<p>and its eigenvectors are <m>v_1 = \left[\begin{array}{c}
-1\cr
-1\cr
-1
\end{array}\right], v_2 = \left[\begin{array}{c}
1\cr
2\cr
1
\end{array}\right]</m> and <m>v_3 = \left[\begin{array}{c}
-2\cr
-2\cr
-1
\end{array}\right]</m>.</p>
<p>The corresponding eigenvalues are <m>\lambda_1 =</m><fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/>, 
<m>\lambda_2 =</m><fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0002"/>, and <m>\lambda_2 =</m><fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0003"/>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-5</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-1</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
